# Boot battery guard (review M2): a cable plugged in while the low-battery
# image is up boots, to the charging flow, instead of powering off (the
# PMU wakes on the charger's edge, which would already be gone, leaving
# the unit dark on the cable). The sim boots at 3,250 mV with no charger
# (under the 3,400 mV floor) and the charger arrives 800 ms after the
# guard's first reading (IPODUI_SIM_CHARGER_AT_MS,
# uisimulator/common/powermgmt-sim.c), inside the 2 s hold.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p16-bootbatt-plug.script
# env: IPODUI_SIM_BATT_MV=3250
# env: IPODUI_SIM_CHARGER_AT_MS=800
# golden: skip
# log: bootbatt refuse mv=3250 thr=3400
# log: sys deadbatt drawn=1
# log: bootbatt plugged mv=3250
# nolog: bootbatt off
# nolog: splash-pass

wait 4000
shot main_menu
